WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned --
and I remember last summer

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were talking a fair amount.
You were so excited

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:06.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be going off to New Zealand
to shoot "Sweet Tooth."

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was New Zealand as wonderful
as you hoped it would be?

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.012 line:92%
-It's -- It is a magical place

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:14.247 line:92%
It's so cool. It's beautiful

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:15.482 line:92%
It's also very interesting

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a lot of
volcanic activity down there

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there are
interesting things, like -

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:23.390
There's this place that I loved.
It's called Kerosene Creek

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's basically
a geothermally warmed river,

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:32.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like having a hot tub
mixed with a river.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.767 size:78% position:39% line:92%
So I went down there.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
My friends Maclain and Clair
were down there,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Libby and I
went down to this creek.

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:41.908 line:92%
And me and my buddy Maclai

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
were doing slow-mo rise-up
through the water.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.381 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Just, you know, just --

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just is the coolest setting
Anyway --

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.418 line:92%
-Here's a good picture, a phot

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
of, like, the sort of
slow-motion action-movie -

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.556 size:84% position:42%
Yeah. That's -- Yeah.
I think we get a sense.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.725 line:92%
-Well, about 20 minutes into u

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.429
trying to get these perfec
"rise out of the water" shot

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.598 line:92%
in slow mo, this guy says,

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
[German accent]
"Excuse me. Uh, I need to --

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think you want to be
doing what you're doing."

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:12.672 line:92%
Yeah, you're not the only on

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
who can do a German accent
Seth.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like,
"What, German tourist?

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.145 line:92%
What are you talking about?"

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.346 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He said, "There are

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:24.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
brain-eating amoebas
in these waters."

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:27.487 line:92%
And we said, "Brain -- What?!"

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:29.556 line:92%
"Amoebas. They eat your brains."

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:30.757 line:92%
And we're like, "Oh, okay.

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we, you know, start digging
the water out of our ears

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.095 line:92%
and make our way to the exit

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:38.932
And he's like, "Oh, I hope
I did not ruin your day."

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Oh, no, no, we --
This has been great.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:46.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
And thanks for waiting friggin
20 minutes to let us know

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:51.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we're dunking our head unde
right in front of you."

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we go up to the front.
We're like,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, well, they've got to
probably have pla--

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
How'd we miss the warning sign
about this?"

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we go up, and there are al
these "don't litter" signs

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Here is an appropriate
place to park."

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.392 line:92%
Nowhere on there is it saying,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Warning.
There's an amoeba down there

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.963 line:92%
that could eat your entire brain

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:13.766
and leave you just, like, yo
know, in a puddle of flesh."

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.236
And so we thought it was a joke,
but we looked it up.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's a real thing.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't happen very often
but still, like,

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:22.742
I think it's at least wort
a casual mention on the sign

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:25.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I feel like that's more
than fair to ask for that.

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:27.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you like
where you ended up staying

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:33.253
'Cause I assume that productio
decided where to put you up.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:36.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I loved
where I was staying.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:39.359 size:81% position:41%
We stayed in Auckland,
but when we went over,

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to quarantine
for two weeks.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:46.032
And we went down. You don't ge
to pick where you quarantine

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
They just put you on a bus
or a plane

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:50.470 line:92%
and send you off to a hotel.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we went to this place
called Rotorua,

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:56.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, again,
a lot of geothermal activity

00:02:56.543 --> 00:02:58.745 line:92%
This is a place that essentially

00:02:58.745 --> 00:03:01.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of all
the geothermal activity,

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
the entire town
smells like farts.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.886 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And it was like,

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:09.856 line:92%
"Oh, these guys know my work."

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.558 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So it was --

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:16.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really an interesting
and cool town,

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.463 line:92%
and you get used to that.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:21.267
But it is something that
your nose has to, you know

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.735 line:92%
contend with for a little bit.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:27.540
-Um, hopefully, you will
allow me this indulgence.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.008 line:92%
The last time you were here,

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
you read a scene
from "MacGruber,"

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
the upcoming series
that will be on Peacock.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
Would you be so kind
as to read us another piec

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:43.289
from this incredibly highl
anticipated television event

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would love to.
And thank you for asking.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.295
I'm gonna put my reading glasses
on because I am old.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.699
So, this is a scene in which
I'm explaining to Kristen Wiig

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:56.169
and Ryan Phillippe's characters,
Vicki and Piper,

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.304 line:92%
the importance of this mission

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's pretty self-explanatory
There are spoilers.

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, what I have done is
I've covered up the spoilers

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.713 size:88% position:44% line:92%
with the word "spoiler."

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:09.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just so --
That's something to know.

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:10.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Okay. Here we go.

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:15.121 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Let me take a little...

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.623 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Vodka in there.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:19.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Red vodka. Okay.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:22.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Piper, why do you think
I hid that spoiler

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a [bleep] spoiler
for 20 years?

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.733 size:81% position:41% line:92%
For gigs and shiggles?

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.734 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
No, I hid it 'cause

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
no government on Earth
should have it.

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:33.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not even the United States
of spoiler.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:36.042
I mean, we're talking abou
a world-ender here, Piper,

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:39.445
and I don't know about you
but I kind of like the world

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:41.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like sunsets.
I like snow-capped mountains

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:45.451
I like kicking back with a col
Molson and watching the game

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:49.455
I like babies and kettle corn,
monster trucks and puppy dogs,

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
tig ol' biddies
and bunchin' mox.

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
I even like cancer
and type II diabetes

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:57.664 size:81% position:41%
because they remind me
that life is precious.

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.965 line:92%
And that's why it is imperativ

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:03.236
that we keep this spoiler
out of spoiler's hands!"

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.737 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:08.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I think
I speak for everyone

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:11.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I say we are
eagerly anticipating this.

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you, dear friend.
I appreciate you making time

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.848 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you very much.
And just so you know,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:16.949 line:92%
it's not just stuff like that.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:20.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's tons of farts
and [bleep] in it, as well

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.988 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Sweet Tooth"
